%erg 0.1
Title: Extend agnostic gate to scripts/ dir
Created: 2026-07-13
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-07-13T20:08Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

`scripts/check-agnostic.sh` scans `skills tickets` by default (CI runs it with
no args). It never scans `scripts/`, so a hardcoded home path in a shell/python
helper escapes every mechanical gate — caught only in human review. The
ticket-0217 seat-runner inherited a hardcoded `HOMEDIR=/home/<user>`; `/gaze`-style
review caught it and it was fixed to `HOMEDIR="$HOME"` in that PR, but the gate
gap remains open for the next regression.

## Discovered blocker (why this is its own ticket)

Extending the default DIRS to include `scripts/` immediately surfaces a
pre-existing violation the ticket-0217 PR should not carry:

    scripts/beat-settings.json:25
      "command": "/home/<user>/.claude/scripts/guard-destructive-bash.sh"

This is a Claude Code hook command. Whether the harness's hook runner expands
`~` or `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` in a hook `command` path is unverified; a blind
rewrite could break beat's destructive-bash guard. That call must be settled
before the gate can go green on `scripts/`.

## Relevant files
- `scripts/check-agnostic.sh` — default DIRS `(skills tickets)`; GLOBAL_PATTERNS
  apply everywhere, SKILL_PATTERNS gated to `skills*` (so `gh`/`uv`/repo-relative
  paths in scripts stay legal — verified).
- `scripts/beat-settings.json` — the pre-existing hardcoded-home violation.
- `.github/workflows/CI.yml` — `agnostic-guard` job runs `check-agnostic.sh`
  with no args (picks up whatever the default DIRS are).
- `Makefile` — `check-agnostic-tickets` / `check-agnostic-skills` targets; a
  `check-agnostic-scripts` target + `check` dep would give local parity.
- `tests/test_check_agnostic.py` — where the scripts/-coverage guard tests land.

## Actions
1. Decide the `beat-settings.json` fix: confirm whether the hook runner expands
   `~`/`$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` in a `command`; if yes, rewrite to an agnostic form;
   if no, either add a JSON-safe exemption or scope the scripts/ scan to code
   files (`*.sh`, `*.py`) so config JSON is out of scope.
2. Add `scripts` to `check-agnostic.sh` default DIRS (or a dedicated
   `check-agnostic-scripts` target wired into `check`).
3. Add regression tests: the real `scripts/` tree is agnostic-clean; a planted
   `/home/<user>` path under a scripts-named dir is caught; skill-only tokens
   (`gh`, `uv run`, `./scripts/x.sh`) do NOT fire in scripts/.

## Test
- `tests/test_check_agnostic.py::test_real_scripts_dir_is_agnostic` — run the
  gate on the actual `scripts/` dir, assert exit 0 (RED until beat-settings.json
  is resolved).

## Invariants
- SKILL_PATTERNS must stay gated to `skills*` — scripts legitimately use `gh`,
  `uv`, and repo-relative paths.
- Do not break beat's destructive-bash guard hook.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `beat-settings.json` hardcoded home path resolved (agnostic form or scoped-out with rationale)
- [ ] `check-agnostic.sh` (or a make target in `check`) scans `scripts/`
- [ ] Regression tests: real scripts/ clean; planted home path caught; skill-only tokens ignored in scripts/
- [ ] `make check` and the CI `agnostic-guard` job pass
